:name: Ethernet traffic probe
:description: Does the emulated MAC actually transmit? Logs the GEM at Noisy while the board brings its interface up.
#
# Note: do NOT use "emulation LogEthernetTraffic" here. It launches Wireshark rather than logging to a
# file, and when Wireshark is absent it raises an error that aborts the rest of the script - which
# silently means the machine never runs and you conclude "no frames" from a run that never happened.

include $tcmodel
include $piomodel
include $rstcmodel
include $usartspimodel
include $afecmodel

mach create "duet3_mb6hc"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $plat

# Renode re-runs the "reset" macro on every machine reset, so the boot vectors are
# re-applied when the firmware resets itself (M999 / DWC reboot). Setting VectorTableOffset
# once outside a macro does not survive: the core would restart on an empty ITCM.
macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadBinary $fw 0x400000
    sysbus LoadSymbolsFrom $elf
    cpu VectorTableOffset 0x400000
    cpu PC `sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x400004`
    cpu SP `sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x400000`
"""
runMacro $reset

emulation CreateSwitch "switch"
connector Connect gem switch

logLevel 3
logLevel -1 gem

emulation RunFor "3.5"
quit
